@MartinDelille you don't need `--headless` (internally --lsp enable headless mode). Also the path to your project is not required.

Ok I make it work by overriding the lsp command just before enabling gdscript:

```lua
		vim.lsp.config.gdscript = {
			cmd = {
				"/path/to/godot.macos.editor.dev.arm64",
				"--lsp",
			},
		}
		vim.lsp.enable("gdscript")
```

Starting it manually doesn't work and I ignore why overriding the cmd in `lsp/gdscript.lua` doesn't works.

It seems to work in the end!
